From: openFyde
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: log an unsupported scanout modifier at
 debug level

rockchip_vop2_mod_supported() is the plane's format_mod_supported hook:
DRM asks it for every plane whenever a client offers a buffer for direct
scanout. The BSP driver answers "no" with DRM_ERROR, so an ordinary
fallback to composition fills the kernel log -- on fydetab_duo, a
fullscreen Notialis window rendered by Mesa 26.2's panfrost (AFBC 32x8
split sparse, 0x0800000000000062, which only the RK3576's VOP3 tables
list) produced eight errors per probe, one for each Esmart and Cluster
window. Upstream's version of this check uses drm_dbg_kms; do the same.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c	2026-10-15 16:56:56.013690004 +0800
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c	2026-10-15 16:56:56.026690466 +0800
@@ -2549,7 +2549,14 @@
 	if (!rockchip_afbc(plane, modifier) &&
 	    !rockchip_rfbc(plane, modifier) &&
 	    !rockchip_tiled(plane, modifier)) {
-		DRM_ERROR("%s unsupported format modifier 0x%llx\n", plane->name, modifier);
+		/*
+		 * Not an error: DRM asks this for every plane when a client
+		 * offers a buffer for scanout, and a modifier the hardware
+		 * cannot scan out simply means "composite it". Upstream logs
+		 * it at debug level too.
+		 */
+		drm_dbg_kms(plane->dev, "%s unsupported format modifier 0x%llx\n",
+			    plane->name, modifier);
 
 		return false;
 	}
